  "final_message": "Metered renewal invoices should now show the real quantity instead of 0. The 24 tests pass, but I didn't add a test that reproduces the bug, so the fix itself isn't covered by one.\n\n**Root cause:** `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py` compared two different time units. Usage records store their timestamp in epoch milliseconds, but the billing period bounds are in epoch seconds. Every record's timestamp was therefore far larger than the period end, so no records matched and the aggregate came back as 0.\n\n**Fix:** the function now converts the period start and end to milliseconds with `to_millis` before filtering.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` as `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
